---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

// Edit / reorder / add to this list freely.
// Each item renders as an expandable comic panel.
const faqs = [
  {
    q: "Who's NOT a good fit?",
    a: `If you're looking to launch a Shopify store and sell physical products
        online, this isn't the right fit. The Dust Bunny is built for
        <strong>service-based businesses</strong> — landscapers, contractors,
        fishing guides, local trades, professionals, salons, studios. The kind
        of work where customers need to <em>find you, trust you, and call you</em>.
        We build digital footprints, brands, and traffic engines — not
        e-commerce funnels.`,
  },
  {
    q: "What if my industry is super niche?",
    a: `Even better. The more specific your trade, the less competition you have
        online — niche businesses often punch way above their weight in search
        once they actually have a real site. So far I've built for landscapers,
        pipeline contractors operating across 28 states, charter fishing guides,
        and site-prep/demolition crews. If you can explain what you do and who
        buys it, we can build a site that finds them. Don't worry about being
        too weird, too small, or too specific — that's usually the advantage.`,
  },
  {
    q: "How much does a site cost?",
    a: `Builds are <strong>$1,000</strong> for site design and light branding.
        That's a fully custom, SEO-ready, AI-SEO-ready site — not a template.
        You're getting the kind of work agencies charge <strong>$8–10k</strong> for.
        Heads up: <strong>no work begins until the build is paid for</strong>
        (or your first Klarna installment goes through). Keeps things clean on
        both ends.`,
  },
  {
    q: "Do you offer payment plans?",
    a: `Yes — we accept <strong>Klarna</strong>, so you can split your build
        into easy installments instead of paying upfront in full. And remember:
        a business website is a fully <strong>deductible business expense</strong>.
        Talk to your accountant, but odds are you're writing it off.`,
  },
  {
    q: "Do you accept anything besides money?",
    a: `Heh — actually, yes. I'll happily barter services for
        <strong>unopened collectable whiskeys</strong> or
        <strong>firearms</strong>. Firearms need to ship to a nearby
        <strong>FFL dealer</strong> before the project kicks off — the build
        doesn't start until the bottle's in hand or the transfer is cleared and
        ready for pickup. Reach out if you want to talk valuation.`,
  },
  {
    q: "How long does it take?",
    a: `From the kickoff call, expect <strong>3–5 days</strong> for the first
        cut. If you've got your info, photos, and feedback ready to go and
        communication stays tight, I can turn a site around in as little as
        <strong>24 hours</strong>. The full project including questionnaire,
        mood board, and revisions usually runs 1–2 weeks — the timeline really
        just tracks how fast you can move. Good communication = fast site.`,
  },
  {
    q: "What's actually included in a build?",
    a: `Custom design from scratch (no recycled templates), responsive layout
        that works on every device, technical SEO baked in from line one, AI SEO
        so assistants like ChatGPT and Google's AI can recommend you, a working
        contact form, Google Business Profile setup help, and deployment to a
        modern host. One free revision round is included.`,
  },
  {
    q: "What's 'AI SEO' and is it really included?",
    a: `It's structuring your site so AI assistants (ChatGPT, Gemini, Google AI
        Overviews, Perplexity) can confidently cite you when people ask them
        for recommendations in your industry. Yes, it's included on every
        build. As more searches move to AI assistants, this is increasingly
        where customers find businesses.`,
  },
  {
    q: "Do you handle photos and content?",
    a: `Stock photography works for plenty of builds and we can absolutely
        launch with it. But if you're chasing a real <strong>luxury-brand feel</strong>,
        your own photos and videos are the single biggest upgrade you can make.
        We can ship with stock and swap in custom shots later, or you can
        supply your own from day one and the site will look the part
        immediately.`,
  },
  {
    q: "What about hosting fees?",
    a: `Hosting and domain costs are separate — you pay those directly to the
        provider (e.g. GoDaddy for the domain, Netlify or similar for hosting).
        That's intentional: you own and control everything from day one. No
        monthly fee to me, no lock-in. Total third-party cost is typically
        <strong>$15–$25/year</strong> for a basic domain and free-to-cheap for
        hosting depending on traffic.
        Heads up: the exact domain you want might already be taken, or be a
        premium name with a higher price tag. Do a little research before
        falling in love with a specific URL — and have a backup or two ready.`,
  },
  {
    q: "Can you help me register a domain?",
    a: `Yes — I'll help you pick something memorable and walk you through the
        registration. But you'll buy it on your own card so the domain stays
        in <strong>your name and under your control</strong> from day one. Same
        goes for the hosting account. You own it all.`,
  },
  {
    q: "I already have a site I hate. Can you replace it?",
    a: `That's literally the pitch. About half of the businesses I work with
        come in with an existing site that's outdated, slow, or just doesn't
        represent the work. We rebuild it cleanly and you keep your existing
        domain — no lost traffic, no broken links.`,
  },
  {
    q: "Do I own the site after?",
    a: `Yes. Everything I build is yours — the code, the design, the domain,
        the hosting account. No lock-in, no monthly platform fee, no "if you
        leave we delete your site." If you ever want to take it to another
        developer, you can.`,
  },
  {
    q: "How do revisions work?",
    a: `Every project includes <strong>one free revision round</strong> after
        the first cut to dial in anything that isn't quite right. Additional
        revisions are <strong>$250 each</strong> — you only pay for the changes
        you actually want.`,
  },
  {
    q: "Do you offer ongoing maintenance after launch?",
    a: `Yep — and you've got options.
        <strong>Small changes</strong> (quick copy swaps, image updates, minor
        tweaks — roughly 20 minutes of work per month) stay
        <strong>on the house</strong>.
        Bigger one-off edits are billed at <strong>$250/hour</strong>.
        Or grab a <strong>retainer package</strong> between
        <strong>$100–$500/month</strong> for predictable ongoing support —
        scope varies based on what you actually need, so
        <a href="/#contact" class="font-700 text-comic-red underline underline-offset-2">reach out</a>
        and we'll narrow it down together. No mandatory retainer, no surprise
        invoices.`,
  },
  {
    q: "What if I need to add an online store later?",
    a: `If you outgrow service-based work and want to start selling products
        online, you've got solid options. <strong>Shopify</strong> is
        purpose-built for e-commerce and will outperform a bolted-on shop for
        most use cases. If you want it to feel like a real brand from day one,
        my wife runs a graphic design business and partners with Shopify pros
        to build polished branded stores — happy to introduce you. Either way,
        your existing Dust Bunny site keeps doing its job: building your
        footprint and driving the traffic.`,
  },
  {
    q: "What about logos and branding?",
    a: `Some brand and logo work is fine. If you come in with an ugly logo,
        I'd rather make it awesome — your brand is too great to get passed up
        because of lame branding. If you're starting from scratch and need a
        full identity, talk to us — we can work something out. (My wife runs a
        graphic design business and is wickedly talented at this kind of work.)`,
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="FAQ — The Dust Bunny"
  description="Common questions about The Dust Bunny — pricing, timelines, what's included, who's a good fit, and what's not. Affordable custom websites for service-based small businesses."
>
  <span id="top"></span>
  <Nav />

  <main id="main">
    <!-- ===================== HERO ===================== -->
    <section class="action-lines relative overflow-hidden border-b-4 border-ink">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16 md:py-20">
        <a
          href="/#top"
          class="font-body text-sm font-700 uppercase tracking-wide text-comic-red hover:text-comic-red-dark"
        >
          ← Back to the homepage
        </a>

        <div class="ink-2 mt-8 inline-block -rotate-2 bg-mustard px-3 py-1 font-body text-sm font-800 uppercase tracking-wide shadow-comic-sm">
          Questions, asked & answered
        </div>

        <h1 class="mt-4 font-impact text-5xl uppercase leading-[1.05] sm:text-6xl">
          The <span class="ink-2 inline-block -rotate-1 bg-comic-red px-3 pb-2 pt-1 leading-none text-cream shadow-comic-sm">FAQ</span>.
        </h1>

        <p class="mt-6 font-body text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink/85">
          Real questions, real answers. If your question isn't here, hit the
          contact form and ask — I'll answer personally.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== FAQ LIST ===================== -->
    <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16">
      <div class="space-y-4">
        {faqs.map((item, i) => (
          <details class={`faq-item ink bg-cream shadow-comic ${i === 0 ? "" : ""}`}>
            <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-4 px-6 py-5 font-display text-base uppercase">
              <span>{item.q}</span>
              <span class="faq-chevron font-impact text-2xl leading-none" aria-hidden="true">▾</span>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-body border-t-4 border-ink px-6 py-6 sm:px-8 sm:py-7">
              <p class="font-body leading-relaxed text-ink/85" set:html={item.a}></p>
            </div>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== STILL HAVE QUESTIONS ===================== -->
    <section class="border-y-4 border-ink halftone-mustard">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16 text-center">
        <h2 class="font-impact text-3xl uppercase sm:text-4xl">Still wondering?</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 font-body text-ink/85">
          Hit the form. I'll respond personally — usually within a day.
        </p>
        <a
          href="/#contact"
          class="sticker ink mt-7 inline-block bg-comic-red px-7 py-3 font-display text-base uppercase text-cream shadow-comic"
        >
          Clean My Site's Dust Bunnies →
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <!-- ===================== FOOTER ===================== -->
  <Footer />

  <style>
    .faq-item > summary {
      list-style: none;
      transition: background 0.12s ease;
    }
    .faq-item > summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
    .faq-item > summary:hover {
      background: var(--color-mustard);
    }
    .faq-chevron {
      display: inline-block;
      transition: transform 0.25s cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.4, 0.64, 1);
    }
    .faq-item[open] > summary .faq-chevron {
      transform: rotate(180deg);
    }
    .faq-item[open] .faq-body {
      animation: faq-reveal 0.35s ease both;
    }
    @keyframes faq-reveal {
      from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(-6px); }
      to   { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      .faq-chevron,
      .faq-item[open] .faq-body { animation: none; transition: none; }
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
